  "description": "T1 - Oak Tree- Growing on the front road-side boundary by the northern entrance- To Remove Deadwood throughout the crown\r Lift the epicormic/lowest growth over the pavement to provide a minimum clearance of 2.5m above ground level\rTo Trim the growth around the streetlamp as necessary to maintain clearance and to allow light to pass through.\rTo thin out the density of this branch to reduce the weight and therefore result in the branch lifting. If this is not sufficient,  cut back this lower branch to clear obstruction to the lamp post\rT2 - Golden False  Acacia - Growing on the southern side of the property- To Crown Reduce by up to 1.5m, on the longest growths to improve shape and size, all to suitable growing points.\rT3 - Dead Cherry Tree- Growing in the back garden- To Fell to as low as possible above existing ground level",
